r Research Centres\nExplore Now\nAthena Swan\nOur Athena Swan Journey\nExplore Now\nSNS Equality, Diversity and Inclusion\nSchool of Natural Sciences EDI\nExplore Now\nNews\nTrinity College Dublin Herbarium Officially Re-opens\nTrinity College Dublin Herbarium, which has been renovated under the Transforming Trinity's Herbarium project, was delighted to officially re-open its doors in a private ceremony with Minister Christopher O'Sullivan.\n18 Sep 2026\nNews\nJohn Joly Memorial Lecture 2026 - Prof Bridget R. Scanlon\nDiscipline of Geology is please to present The John Joly Memorial Lecture 2026 which will be delivered by Prof Bridget R. Scanlon\n08 Oct 2026\nEvent, News\nPost Doctoral Research Fellow Opportunity\nCurrent Research Fellow Vacancies: Research Fellow - CMAP (Coastal Monitoring and Adaptation Planning) research project as part of the Trinity Coastal Research Group based in Discipline of Geography.\n28 Sep 2026\nEducation, News\nMore News & Events\nOur Mission\nOur mission is to cultivate an academic environment that supports and enables excellence in education, research, and public service.\nOur Vision\nOur vision is to be a national and global leader at the intersection of the natural sciences, society and the environment...\nOur Values\nWe value being able to do our educational and research activities freely in a safe, supportive, cooperative, and well-resourced working environment...\nQuick Links\nAlumni & Friends\nOur diverse alumni community comprises almost 9,000 graduates worldwide.\nGradLink Testimonials\nHear from our Graduates.\nResearch Highlights\nView a selection of recent accomplishments from around our School.\nCurrent Vacancies\nFor details of the latest vacancies within School of Natural Sciences.\nUndergraduate Fieldtrips Payments\nMasters fieldtrips payment\nNaturalScience\nHome\nContact\nUpdated 8 October 2026\nTrinity College Dublin, The University of Dublin.\nCollege Green, Dublin 2, Ireland\nT: +353 1 896 1000\nTrinity Association